{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Subscriber lab: test the resource boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SPS-PRIVATE-DEMO-20261022"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This saved Website Builder Widget is the protected lab for the article. Its Article relation is private, and the Article explicitly references a subscription Product. Read it with a current owned paid period and Role grant, then repeat with another Subject and without a JWT. The private Widget and its descendants must be denied in the latter cases."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Check the same requests immediately before the fixed period ends, exactly at its deadline and after Role revocation. Keep the marker inside this protected Widget only when inspecting page HTML and API responses. The public article explains the architecture; access to these saved lab records remains subject to the server guard."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A controlled revocation walkthrough"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use disposable local Subjects, an accepted paid period and a Role relation belonging to that fixture. Keep the operator credential out of the content read: an operator bypass would hide the denial this exercise needs to verify. The reading token belongs to the entitled Subject, including a guest Subject with no login Identity."}]},{"type":"codeBlock","attrs":{"language":"ts"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { api as subjectApi } from
  "@sps/rbac/models/subject/sdk/server";
import { api as subjectRolesApi } from
  "@sps/rbac/relations/subjects-to-roles/sdk/server";

const localApiOrigin = "http://localhost:4000";
const read = () => subjectApi
  .blogModuleArticleFindByIdContentFind({
    host: localApiOrigin,
    id: fixtureSubjectId,
    blogModuleArticleId: fixtureArticleId,
    options: { headers: {
      Authorization: "Bearer " + fixtureJwt,
      "Cache-Control": "no-store",
    } },
  });

const before = await read();
if (before.access.state !== "granted") throw Error("Fixture is not entitled");
await subjectRolesApi.delete({
  host: localApiOrigin,
  id: fixtureGrantId,
  options: { headers: { "X-RBAC-SECRET-KEY": localOperatorSecret } },
});
const after = await read();
if (after.access.state === "granted") throw Error("Revocation did not apply");"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fixture variables are inputs from your isolated setup, not values copied from a live account. Save the granted Widget ID before revocation and request it directly afterward: its by-ID read must fail. Filter list and count by that exact protected Widget ID; the results must be an empty list and zero. An unfiltered collection can still contain public records. Repeat with the managed File content endpoint and exact File ID if the fixture contains a private file. A public Article title can stay readable throughout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run the existing proceed retry tests after removing the grant. An ordinary retry or automatic renewal on a revoked Order must not silently restore the grant. The integration fixture also compares the instant before expiry with the exact deadline using its controlled server clock; do not extend a period through a generic user PATCH to make the fixture pass."}]}]}

